; lang.xon -- what this bundle is.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every manifest
; in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon). An unknown form is a loud
; error, never a silent skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a requirement
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (requires-lang "NAME" ["V"]) another lang this one is written on top
;                               of, optionally at an exact version
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "logo")

; Radon, read off the imports rather than chosen:
;
;   x/sys/socket   the viewer is served over TCP (serve.x)
;   x/sys/file     the bytecode file the viewer polls, and LOAD's filein
;   x/sys/posix    fork, kill, wait, signal -- main.x runs the server as a
;                  child and reaps it when the REPL exits
;
; Those three are radon opt-ins; a helium Logo would boot and die on the first
; import. A headless Logo emitting bytecode to stdout would need none of them,
; but that would be a second bundle, not a flag on this one -- (dialect ...) is
; a requirement, not a taste negotiated at load time.
(dialect rn)

; The x-lang release this bundle is built and tested against; CI compares it
; for equality. The floor is set by one door: (Type named ...), which
; logo/state.x fetches the platform's type handles through and which no
; release before v0.15.0 provides.
(requires-release "v0.26.0")

(entry "run.x")
